    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite (2 tests in `AcceptanceTest`; the other files are the abstract base and a helper) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived `membershipTier` to the owner representation.\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getMembershipTier()` derived getter alongside the existing `getMembershipNumber()`, keeping the tier logic in the domain model where the fields it depends on (`namesakeCount`, `email`) live:\n   ```java\n   public String getMembershipTier() {\n       boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isEmpty();\n       boolean noNamesakes = this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0;\n       return (noNamesakes && hasEmail) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` property (enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec, and MapStruct's `toOwnerDto` maps the new field automatically from the matching getter \u2014 no mapper or controller changes needed.\n\nThe logic returns `SILVER` only when `namesakeCount == 0` and a non-empty email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise (including when `namesakeCount` is null/absent), matching the specification and both acceptance tests.",
